  "details": "While testing the new public instance domain allowlist, I found a case where the client log stated the URL was not allowed, but it was actually playing the video. I don't have much info other than a screenshot of the log. It happened while testing issues reported [here](https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/even-if-i-set-an-untursted-domain-the-video-player-still-gives-me-an-error) and I'm not sure whether the involved domains were on the allowlist at the time... regardless, something weird happened.\n\nThis happened in https://vrchat.com/home/launch?worldId=wrld_36349389-4795-46ab-aded-71d73208d3fa\n\nYou can make it play a video by clicking the power button on the game console at spawn.\n\nNote: the fmc-pc.vrc.natalie.ee URL 302 redirects to a vrchat-fmc-pc.cdn.natalie.ee URL.",
